  "gaps": [
    "The docs tie no specific card number to an outcome. The outcome comes from cardholder name, CVV and expiry month on any valid card. So every Mexico card has the same approved and declined field sets. The repo preset that labels 5204740000002745 as the 'declined' Mastercard is not supported by the docs: that card is simply listed under MASTERCARD Credit Card for Mexico.",
    "The test page states no cardholder name value for PENDING. Pending is only documented through the antifraud emails pending_approved@payu.com and pending_rejected@payu.com.",
    "The expiry examples in the docs use a placeholder (05/202_, 07/202_). Month exactly 6 is not covered by either rule.",
    "The test page gives no document or ID rule for Mexico. The Payments API Mexico page was not fetched.",
    "The response-codes HTML table wraps a few long codes with a stray space (e.g. 'CREDIT_CARD_NOT_AUTHORIZED _FOR_INTERNET_TRANSACTIONS', 'INVALID_EXPIRATION_DATE_OR _SECURITY_CODE'). The literal is recorded without the space. Confirm against a real API response.",
    "polResponseCode values come from the 'Response Codes Sent to the Response URL' table. BANK_UNREACHABLE's polResponseCode was cut off in the extract and is omitted.",
    "The docs give no retry guidance except REPEAT_TRANSACTION ('You must repeat the transaction'). retryable=true on network and provider errors is an inference from category processing_error."
  ]
}
